/**
@example main.c
@details A word counter built on the single header, dist/mule.h. The file
lives in a Str inside an Arena, and every line and word is a StrView into it.

@example 01_build.c
@details Build a Str with appends that chain with `&&`, print it two ways,
free it.

@example 02_reuse.c
@details Clear and refill one Str in a loop, so one allocation serves every
pass.

@example 03_file.c
@details Read a whole file into a Str, and tell a read error from out of
memory.

@example 04_views.c
@details Trim, find and slice a StrView without allocating, and see why `%s`
is the wrong way to print one.

@example 05_split.c
@details Split fields with sv_split_next() and words with sv_token_next(),
and see how they treat empty pieces.

@example 06_sort.c
@details Sort an array of StrViews with qsort and sv_cmp().

@example 07_lines.c
@details One Str owns a whole novel, and views walk its 22,750 lines without
a single further allocation.

@example 08_keep.c
@details Copy a view into a Str of its own when the text must outlive the
buffer it came from.

@example 09_replace.c
@details Write your own function in the library's shape: StrViews in, a Str
to append to, a `bool` out.

@example 10_dangling.c
@details A bug on purpose. A view kept across an append that moves the
buffer reads freed memory.

@example 11_double_free.c
@details A bug on purpose. Copying a Str struct makes two owners of one
buffer.
*/
